# Used by Dockerfile.mapproxy (context .). An allowlist: everything is left
# out of the build context except the two files the Dockerfile COPYs
# (mapproxy/environment.yml and mapproxy/docker/app.py). A list of what to
# exclude never keeps up with the repository -- site/, site-docs/, images/
# and a local .venv/ are all large and were all being sent to the Docker
# daemon on every build -- whereas a new file the image needs fails the
# build at once with "not found".
#
# Add a `!path` line here whenever Dockerfile.mapproxy gets a new COPY.
# Bind-mounted at Compose runtime, never copied into an image: the MBTiles
# under tileserver/data (hundreds of GB, which would stall the upload),
# tileserver/{config,fonts,styles}, mapproxy/{config,data,locks,tile_locks}
# and nginx.
*
!mapproxy/environment.yml
!mapproxy/docker/app.py
